TzD (task #42): self-relative references as integer arithmetic.
alternative.c, callthunks.c and runtime-const.h reach code from a table entry by
adding the entry's own address to the offset it holds, as pointer
arithmetic: the result lies outside the entry, which is undefined in C
and traps in TzD (the pointer keeps the table's bounds).  The kernel's
own offset_to_ptr(), jump_entry_code(), ex_to_insn() and
static_call_addr() do the same sum on unsigned long; written that way
here too, the result is an address made from an integer (in kernel
mode, bounded by its region: the kernel image).
